  "attribution": "Written by a model from the explanatory memorandum; not the record",
  "describes_version": "original",
  "as_of": "2023-09-14",
  "sentences": [
   "The bill would repeal the Disability Services Act 1986 and update other Commonwealth laws to support its replacement by a new disability services framework.",
   "It would preserve existing grant agreements under the former legislation until they end, while new grants and financial arrangements would use the replacement framework.",
   "The repeal and related changes would commence with the Disability Services and Inclusion Act 2023, supported by saving provisions for existing programs and entitlements."
  ],
  "changes": [
   "Existing disability services payments would retain their income tax exemption.",
   "Hearing Australia's duties would refer to the new framework's objects and principles.",
   "New instrument-making powers would identify employment supports relevant to pension and mobility allowance eligibility."
  ],
  "affected": "People with disability and the organisations funded under grant agreements to provide supports and services for them are affected.",
